+# Recorded-call scoring
+
+How `tracer score` compares the transcript export of a recorded call with a speech-to-text transcript of its audio, and what that comparison does and does not say. Decisions: [ADR 0023](../adr/0023-recorded-call-agreement-scoring.md), [ADR 0024](../adr/0024-provider-adapters-byok-sarvam-rest.md), [ADR 0025](../adr/0025-marathi-comparison-normaliser.md).
+
+## What is measured
+
+- Tracer measures the agreement between the agent's transcript export of a call and an independent speech-to-text transcript of the same audio.
+- The value is labelled agreement distance (MER): the measure of Morris, Maier and Green (2004), computed over word counts H, S, D and I (hits, substitutions, deletions, insertions). It is 0 when the two texts agree word for word and never above 1.
+- Every number is printed with its counts and its denominator, for example "9 of 120 export tokens are flagged".
+- The report points at spans where the two texts disagree. A span is flagged when its confidence reaches the parameter flag_min_confidence of the rubric file, which has no default.
+- The confidence of a flag is the character edit distance of the two span keys over the longer key, and it is uncalibrated.
+- The confidence is not a probability.
+
+## Not claimed
+
+- A flag is not a claim that the export holds an error, and a flag may be where the speech-to-text engine is wrong.
+- An unflagged span is not shown to be right: it only means the two texts agree there.
+- The export is not a reference or ground truth, and neither is the speech-to-text transcript.
+- Two clips are a demonstration, not a validation (BL-170); no number computed from them supports a general claim.
+
+```text
+Tracer reports how far two transcripts agree; it does not measure accuracy, and none of its numbers is a WER, a CER, an error rate, a recall or a precision.
+```
+
+## Scope, roles and tier
+
+- Only Marathi (language code mr, in Devanagari) is in scope in this release.
+- The language is declared by you with --declared-language; Tracer does not infer it from the export.
+- The caller is never evaluated. What is judged is the agent's text.
+- The caller lines of the export are the agent's own recognition of the caller, so they are agent output.
+- The speech-to-text turns have role unknown, because Tracer does no speaker separation.
+- The report labels each flag with the role of its export turn.
+- A recorded run is at tier T0: the export and the audio are the only evidence.
+
+## Cost
+
+- Without a USD price the cost is not_available, with its reason.
+- A missing cost is never 0.
+
+## Privacy and consent
+
+- The audio leaves your machine only with --stt sarvam, and only to Sarvam.
+- With --stt fake:DIR the replay sends nothing and needs no key.
+- The report and the store hold call text, so they must stay out of git.
+- The call log holds no text: it holds counts, ids and timings.
+- Put --out outside the repository.
+- A consent record is given with --consent, --consent-reference and --consent-recorded-at.
+- Retention is recorded and not enforced: nothing deletes the files after the retention date (BL-234).
+- Embedding the audio in the report with --embed-audio is opt-in, and the file then holds personal data.
+
+## Run book
+
+- Before a real send follow the Run book for a real send in ADR 0024.
+- Do a dry run first, with the arguments of the real send.
+- The --max-chunks ceiling refuses a plan with more chunks than you allowed.
+- For the offline quick start on the synthetic pair see packages/cli/README.md.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Number words against digits are not folded, so a number spoken as a word and written in digits can be flagged (BL-192).
+- A two-letter word flags exactly at the threshold when one letter differs, a three-letter word does not.
+- A split word, one space inserted into a word, stays below the threshold and is not flagged.
+- The noise floor of the speech-to-text run is unmeasured until P3-31.
+- No native review of the Marathi results has happened (BL-169), and the agreement scale is the owner's principle (BL-165).
+
+## Related
+
+- [Offline quick start and exit codes](../../packages/cli/README.md)
+- [The synthetic pair](../examples/synthetic-mr/README.md)
+- [ADR 0023](../adr/0023-recorded-call-agreement-scoring.md)
+- [ADR 0024](../adr/0024-provider-adapters-byok-sarvam-rest.md)
+- [ADR 0025](../adr/0025-marathi-comparison-normaliser.md)
+
+The page is checked by `test_concept_page_states_no_accuracy_claim`.
