+# Measurement report: <title>
+
+Copy this file to `docs/phase3/measurements/<name>.md`, fill every placeholder, and change the status. A report names clips by id only (clip-A, clip-B) and holds counts, never text.
+
+## Scope and status
+
+Status: template
+Date: <date>
+Task: P3-31
+
+## Clips
+
+Clips are named by id only: clip-A and clip-B.
+
+| Clip | Export turns | Export tokens | Audio seconds |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| clip-A | <n> | <n> | <seconds> |
+| clip-B | <n> | <n> | <seconds> |
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Setting | Value |
+|---|---|
+| flag_min_confidence | <value> |
+| normaliser | <value> |
+| max_chunk_ms | <value> |
+| search_ms | <value> |
+| stt_model_as_requested | <value> |
+| r3_shift_ms | <value> |
+
+## Counts per run
+
+In a cell 'N of D', N is the numerator and D the denominator; the decimal in brackets is N divided by D.
+
+| Run | Clip | Chunks answered (n of d) | Attempts | Export tokens | STT tokens | H | S | D | I | Agreement distance (MER) (n of d) | Flags | Flagged export tokens (n of d) | Export turns with a flag (n of d) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| R1 | clip-A | <n> of <d> | <n> | <n> | <n> | <n> | <n> | <n> | <n> | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) | <n> | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) |
+
+## Usage and cost
+
+Cost is not_available when no USD price is given, and it is never written as 0.
+
+| Run | Clip | Requests | Audio seconds | Cost |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| R1 | clip-A | <n> | <seconds> | not_available (<reason>) |
+
+## Flags per run
+
+| Run | Clip | Flags | Flag span ids |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| R1 | clip-A | <n> | <ids> |
+
+## Run-to-run difference
+
+Jaccard is the flagged tokens in both runs over the flagged tokens in either run.
+R2 repeats R1 with the same inputs and R3 shifts the chunk boundaries by half a window.
+The normaliser row compares the stored data scored with the normaliser on and off, offline.
+
+| Comparison | Clip | Flagged tokens in both | Flagged tokens in either | Jaccard (n of d) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| R1 vs R2 | clip-A | <n> | <n> | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) |
+| R1 vs R3 | clip-A | <n> | <n> | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) |
+| R1 normaliser on vs off | clip-A | <n> | <n> | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) |
+| R1 vs R2 | clip-B | <n> | <n> | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) |
+| R1 vs R3 | clip-B | <n> | <n> | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) |
+| R1 normaliser on vs off | clip-B | <n> | <n> | <n> of <d> (<ratio>) |
+
+## What was NOT measured
+
+- Native-speaker review of any flag or of the normaliser (BL-169).
+- Anything beyond two clips: this is a demonstration (BL-170).
+- Any other speech-to-text engine, model or language.
+
+## Not claimed
+
+```text
+Tracer reports how far two transcripts agree; it does not measure accuracy, and none of its numbers is a WER, a CER, an error rate, a recall or a precision.
+```
