 # tracer-cli
 
-The `tracer` command line. Status: 0.0.1, scaffold only (`tracer --help`).
+The `tracer` command line, version 0.0.1: `tracer score` compares the agent's transcript export of a recorded call with a speech-to-text transcript of its audio and points at the spans where the two disagree. Concepts and limits: [recorded-call scoring](../../docs/concepts/recorded-call-scoring.md).
+
+## Quick start (offline, no key, no network)
+
+Run these commands from the repository root, with the workspace installed (`uv sync --locked --all-groups`). They score the invented Marathi pair of `docs/examples/synthetic-mr` against scripted speech-to-text replies. The work directory is created outside the repository, because the output holds call text.
+
+```sh
+WORK="$(mktemp -d)"
+python -I docs/examples/synthetic-mr/make_wav.py "$WORK/synthetic_mr.wav"
+mkdir -p "$WORK/replay"
+cp docs/examples/synthetic-mr/stt_chunk_00.json "$WORK/replay/chunk-0000.json"
+cp docs/examples/synthetic-mr/stt_chunk_01.json "$WORK/replay/chunk-0001.json"
+cp docs/examples/synthetic-mr/stt_chunk_02.json "$WORK/replay/chunk-0002.json"
+uv run --locked tracer score "$WORK/synthetic_mr.wav" \
+  --transcript docs/examples/synthetic-mr/export_synthetic_mr.txt \
+  --rubric docs/examples/rubric-mr.example.json \
+  --declared-language mr \
+  --caller-origin simulated \
+  --consent unknown \
+  --retention keep \
+  --out "$WORK/out" \
+  --stt "fake:$WORK/replay"
+```
+
+The replay folder holds one file per chunk named `chunk-NNNN.json` (four digits). Expected output (lines with a name in angle brackets differ from run to run; the exit code is 0):
+
+```text
+result: scored
+language declared by user: mr
+agreement distance (MER): 0.10655737704918032 (13 of 122; H 109, S 9, D 2, I 2)
+tokens: 120 in the export, 120 in the stt transcript
+flags: 8 (confidence at or above 0.5)
+flagged share of export tokens: 9 of 120 (0.075)
+export turns with a flag: 7 of 22
+cost: not available (no_usage)
+store: <out>/tracer.sqlite
+```
+
+## Exit codes
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| 0 | scored |
+| 1 | unexpected failure |
+| 2 | not scored |
+| 3 | speech-to-text failed |
+| 4 | input refused |
+| 64 | usage |
+
+## Privacy and a real send
+
+- The audio leaves your machine only with --stt sarvam, to Sarvam.
+- The key SARVAM_API_KEY is read from the environment or from --env-file and is never on the command line.
+- With fake: a replay sends nothing.
+- The report and the store hold call text and must stay out of git; put --out outside the repository.
+- Every privacy and language option is required and none has a default.
+- Before a real send follow the Run book for a real send of ADR 0024: [run book](../../docs/adr/0024-provider-adapters-byok-sarvam-rest.md).
+- What the numbers mean and do not mean: [concept page](../../docs/concepts/recorded-call-scoring.md).
